@*
    The shell. ⚠️ There is deliberately no @rendermode anywhere in this file or in Routes:
    static SSR is the default and interactivity is opted into per component (§3.11 C12).
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["theme.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["BurmesePoker.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes />

    @*
        🔥 OUR RECONNECT OVERLAY, NOT THE FRAMEWORK'S (§3.11 C16, BUILD-PLAN P13.5).

        Blazor ships one if you do not, and it is the ugliest screen in the app: a hard-coded
        light-theme modal that ignores prefers-color-scheme, and — the real problem — it leaves
        the page underneath live. `main` is not inert, every button stays focusable and
        pressable, and focus never enters the dialog. So during an outage a player can tab to a
        card and press it, and nothing happens, and nothing says why.

        §3.11 C16 says reconnection is UX and not an error path. This is that, taken seriously:
        the themed palette, a real dialog that focus moves into, the page behind it made inert,
        and a plain <a href=""> to reload — which needs no circuit, because there isn't one.

        ⚠️ It is NOT a live region. The round log is the only one on the page (§3.11 B8), and a
        second one competing with it during an outage is exactly the wrong moment for two voices.
        Focus moving into the dialog is what announces it.

        The element id and the four class names are Blazor's contract; the markup inside is ours.
    *@
    <div id="components-reconnect-modal"
         class="reconnect"
         role="dialog"
         aria-modal="true"
         aria-labelledby="reconnect-heading"
         tabindex="-1">
        <div class="panel">
            <h2 id="reconnect-heading">
                <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">⚡</span>
                The table is still there
            </h2>

            <p class="rejoining">
                Your connection dropped. Rejoining —
                attempt <span id="components-reconnect-current-attempt"></span>
                of <span id="components-reconnect-max-retries"></span>.
            </p>

            <p class="failed">
                Could not get back to the table. The seat is still yours and the computer has
                been playing it (RULES.md §7.2 — nothing ends a match).
            </p>

            <p class="rejected">
                The table moved on without this page. Reload to pick it up again.
            </p>

            <p class="controls">
                <a href="" class="reload">Reload the page</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    @*
        The half a dialog cannot do in CSS: take the page behind it out of reach, and put the
        caret inside it. Blazor toggles the classes; this watches for that and does the rest.
        ⚠️ Vanilla, at the end of the body, and deliberately not a component — a circuit that has
        dropped cannot render the thing that says the circuit has dropped.
    *@
    <script>
        (function () {
            var modal = document.getElementById('components-reconnect-modal');

            if (!modal) {
                return;
            }

            var showing = ['components-reconnect-show', 'components-reconnect-failed', 'components-reconnect-rejected'];
            var was = false;

            function settle() {
                var up = showing.some(function (name) { return modal.classList.contains(name); });

                Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.body.children, function (child) {
                    if (child !== modal && child.tagName !== 'SCRIPT') {
                        child.inert = up;
                    }
                });

                if (up && !was) {
                    modal.focus();
                }

                was = up;
            }

            new MutationObserver(settle).observe(modal, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['class'] });
            settle();
        })();
    </script>

    @*
        🔥 Copying a table's link — the one thing on the lobby a browser cannot do with a real
        control (BUILD-PLAN P54). The link beside it is an <a> and works without any of this;
        this only adds the button.

        ⚠️ Delegated from the document and marked on the document, deliberately. Enhanced
        navigation replaces the page's markup without reloading, so a script that wired each
        button at load would leave dead buttons behind the first time somebody came back to the
        lobby. The class is what the stylesheet reveals the buttons with, so a browser without
        the clipboard API — or with the script blocked — shows no button rather than a broken one.
    *@
    <script>
        (function () {
            if (!navigator.clipboard) {
                return;
            }

            document.documentElement.classList.add('can-copy');

            document.addEventListener('click', function (pressed) {
                var button = pressed.target.closest('[data-copy]');

                if (!button) {
                    return;
                }

                navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy).then(function () {
                    var said = button.textContent;

                    button.textContent = 'Copied';
                    setTimeout(function () { button.textContent = said; }, 1500);
                });
            });
        })();
    </script>

    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
